---
title: "Stats"
description: "Every number this site knows about itself – posts, notes, words, GitHub, books, projects, bookmarks. All computed fresh at build time."
date: 2026-11-01
image: /img/og/stats.jpeg
---

{#- All page CSS lives here: this page alone uses these rules, so they do not
    belong in the shared stylesheet. Everything reads the global theme
    variables, so the page keeps its look in light, paper, and dark. -#}
<style>
  .stats {
    /* The accent drives every bar, fill and heatmap cell on this page, so the
       whole thing retints when a theme changes its link color. */
    --stats-accent: var(--text-color-link);
    --stats-accent-soft: color-mix(in srgb, var(--text-color-link) 45%, transparent);
    --stats-accent-faint: color-mix(in srgb, var(--text-color-link) 22%, transparent);
    --stats-accent-strong: color-mix(in srgb, var(--text-color-link) 72%, transparent);
    --stats-empty: color-mix(in srgb, var(--text-color-muted) 13%, transparent);

    /* Five-step ramp for the month map. The step count matches the quantile
       buckets computed in _data/siteStats.js. */
    --heat-1: color-mix(in srgb, var(--text-color-link) 16%, transparent);
    --heat-2: color-mix(in srgb, var(--text-color-link) 32%, transparent);
    --heat-3: color-mix(in srgb, var(--text-color-link) 46%, transparent);
    --heat-4: color-mix(in srgb, var(--text-color-link) 74%, transparent);
    --heat-5: var(--text-color-link);

    /* Ink for the fourth step, which lands on a mid-tone blue in every theme
       and is the one place the two obvious choices both fail. Measured white
       on light-theme step 4 is 3.13:1, so light needs dark ink; paper's accent
       is dark enough that it needs light ink; and in the dark theme the ramp
       runs the other way, so the surface colour is already the dark one. No
       single token covers all three, so the flip is declared per theme the
       same way the site declares its own. */
    --heat-4-ink: var(--text-color);
  }

  html[data-theme="paper"] .stats,
  html[data-theme="dark"] .stats {
    --heat-4-ink: var(--surface-color);
  }

  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    html:not([data-theme]) .stats {
      --heat-4-ink: var(--surface-color);
    }
  }

  /* Anchored headings must clear the sticky header when jumped to. */
  .stats [id] {
    scroll-margin-top: 5rem;
  }

  /* One line under each h2 saying what the section answers, so a number is
     never presented without its question. */
  .section-intro {
    margin: 0.35rem 0 1.1rem;
    color: var(--text-color-muted);
  }

  /* ---- Hero ---- */

  /* The page needs one entry point. Everything else is a supporting figure, and
     the type scale should say so before a single label is read. */
  .stats-hero {
    margin: 1.75rem 0 1.5rem;
  }

  .hero-figure {
    display: block;
    font-size: clamp(3.25rem, 13vw, 5.25rem);
    line-height: 0.92;
    font-weight: 650;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    color: var(--text-color-link);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  .hero-label {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 3.5vw, 1.3rem);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .hero-note {
    margin: 0.7rem 0 0;
    max-width: 46ch;
    color: var(--text-color-muted);
  }

  /* ---- Supporting figures ---- */

  /* Unboxed on purpose: three quiet figures under the hero, separated by a rule
     rather than three more borders. */
  .stat-row {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 1.75rem 0 0;
    padding: 1.25rem 0 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-color);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(160px, 100%), 1fr));
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  .stat-row a {
    display: block;
    max-width: none;
    text-decoration: none;
    color: inherit;
  }

  .stat-row-fig {
    display: block;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.1;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  .stat-row a:hover .stat-row-fig,
  .stat-row a:focus-visible .stat-row-fig {
    color: var(--text-color-link);
  }

  .stat-row-label {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 0.25rem;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: var(--text-color-muted);
  }

  .stat-row-sub {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 0.35rem;
    font-family: var(--font-family-monospace);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    color: var(--text-color-soft);
  }

  /* ---- Cards (kept for things that are targets) ---- */

  .collection-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 520px) {
    .collection-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }

  .stat-card {
    padding: 1.15rem 1.25rem 1rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: var(--surface-color);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.3rem;
    /* Each card is a query container, so its contents respond to the width of
       the card itself rather than to the viewport. The same card is used at
       three different widths on this page, so a viewport breakpoint would be
       guessing at all three. */
    container-type: inline-size;
  }

  .stat-number {
    font-size: 1.75rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text-color-link);
    line-height: 1.1;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  @container (max-width: 200px) {
    .stat-number {
      font-size: 1.45rem;
    }
  }

  .stat-label {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--text-color-muted);
  }

  .stat-sub {
    font-family: var(--font-family-monospace);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    color: var(--text-color-soft);
  }

  /* A card that is a link keeps the card look but gains affordance: the whole
     surface is the target, and the label carries the underline on hover. */
  a.stat-card {
    text-decoration: none;
    color: inherit;
    /* The global `body a { max-width: fit-content }` would shrink each card to
       its text; a card in a grid has to fill its column. */
    max-width: none;
  }

  a.stat-card:hover,
  a.stat-card:focus-visible {
    border-color: var(--stats-accent-soft);
  }

  a.stat-card:hover .stat-label,
  a.stat-card:focus-visible .stat-label {
    color: var(--text-color-link);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }

  /* ---- Panels (borderless grouping) ---- */

  /* Charts and figure lists are not click targets, so they do not need a boxed
     surface. A hairline and whitespace group them at a fraction of the visual
     weight, which leaves the boxed card meaning "this one is a link". */
  .panel-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(290px, 100%), 1fr));
    gap: 1.5rem 2.25rem;
  }

  .panel-grid--stack {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }

  .panel {
    padding-top: 1.1rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-color);
  }

  .panel h3 {
    margin: 0 0 0.9rem;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .figure-list {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.6rem;
  }

  .figure-list li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr;
    column-gap: 1rem;
    align-items: baseline;
  }

  .figure-key {
    font-family: var(--font-family-monospace);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    color: var(--text-color-soft);
  }

  .figure-val {
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  /* In a full-width panel the key/value list becomes a row of stat columns:
     label on top, figure underneath. */
  .panel-grid--stack .figure-list {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(130px, 1fr));
    gap: 1.1rem 1rem;
  }

  .panel-grid--stack .figure-list li {
    display: block;
  }

  .panel-grid--stack .figure-key {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 0.2rem;
  }

  .panel-grid--stack .figure-val {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
  }

  .card-note {
    margin: 0.85rem 0 0;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    color: var(--text-color-soft);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  /* ---- Reference tier ---- */

  /* Lookup material rather than narrative: same information, deliberately
     quieter, so the eye can tell at a glance what is worth reading. */
  .reference {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  .reference h3 {
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: var(--text-color-muted);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  /* ---- Writing life map ---- */

  /* The map is a real table: a month is a row-and-column intersection, screen
     readers get proper headers, and every cell that has entries links to that
     month on the archive. Colour is a second channel on top of the number, not
     the only one, so nothing here depends on hovering. */
  .cal-wrap {
    overflow-x: auto;
  }

  /* The global stylesheet sets `table { display: block }` for horizontal
     scrolling; these two tables do their own scrolling in a wrapper, so they
     need real table layout back or the columns collapse to content width. */
  /* Below 40em the global stylesheet gives every table `margin: 0 1rem` and
     `min-width: 100%`, meant to pair with `.table-wrapper`'s negative margins.
     These tables use their own wrappers, so they would inherit the side margins
     without the compensation and overflow their container by 2rem on exactly
     the screens with the least room. */
  .cal-table,
  .stats-table {
    margin: 0;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .cal-table {
    display: table;
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: separate;
    border-spacing: 4px;
    table-layout: fixed;
  }

  /* The global table rules add a rule line under every th and td; the map draws
     its own separation with the cell gaps. */
  .cal-table th,
  .cal-table td {
    border: 0;
  }

  /* Global zebra striping would band the map behind the cells. */
  .cal-table tbody tr {
    background: none;
  }

  .cal-table th {
    font-family: var(--font-family-monospace);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 0.66rem;
    color: var(--text-color-soft);
    padding: 0;
  }

  .cal-table thead th {
    text-align: center;
  }

  .cal-table tbody th {
    text-align: left;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    color: var(--text-color-muted);
    width: 3rem;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .cal-table tbody th a {
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .cal-table tbody th a:hover,
  .cal-table tbody th a:focus-visible {
    color: var(--text-color-link);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .cal-table td {
    padding: 0;
    height: 2.4rem;
  }

  .cal-cell {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    height: 100%;
    border-radius: 4px;
    background: var(--stats-empty);
    font-family: var(--font-family-monospace);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    color: var(--text-color-soft);
    text-decoration: none;
    max-width: none;
    /* Keep the map readable on paper: browsers drop background colour by
       default when printing. */
    -webkit-print-color-adjust: exact;
    print-color-adjust: exact;
  }

  /* The two strongest steps invert onto the surface colour rather than a fixed
     white: the accent is a deep blue in the light themes and a pale one in the
     dark theme, so a hardcoded white would fail contrast in exactly one. */
  .cal-cell--c1 { background: var(--heat-1); color: var(--text-color); }
  .cal-cell--c2 { background: var(--heat-2); color: var(--text-color); }
  .cal-cell--c3 { background: var(--heat-3); color: var(--text-color); }
  .cal-cell--c4 { background: var(--heat-4); color: var(--heat-4-ink); }
  .cal-cell--c5 { background: var(--heat-5); color: var(--surface-color); }

  a.cal-cell:hover,
  a.cal-cell:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--text-color-link);
    outline-offset: 1px;
  }

  .cal-total {
    font-family: var(--font-family-monospace);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text-color-muted);
    text-align: right;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    width: 2.6rem;
  }

  .cal-legend {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    column-gap: 1rem;
    row-gap: 0.4rem;
    margin-top: 0.9rem;
    font-family: var(--font-family-monospace);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    color: var(--text-color-soft);
  }

  .cal-legend span {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.35rem;
  }

  .cal-legend b {
    width: 10px;
    height: 10px;
    border-radius: 2px;
    -webkit-print-color-adjust: exact;
    print-color-adjust: exact;
  }

  .cal-readout {
    margin: 0.9rem 0 0;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--text-color-soft);
  }

  /* Under 560px twelve numerals will not fit at a readable size, so the map
     drops to colour only and keeps its full width instead of scrolling
     sideways. Each cell keeps its aria-label, so the counts are still
     announced, and every month is still a link into the archive. */
  @media (max-width: 559px) {
    .cal-wrap {
      overflow-x: visible;
    }

    .cal-table {
      border-spacing: 3px;
    }

    .cal-num {
      display: none;
    }

    .cal-table td {
      height: 1.6rem;
    }

    .cal-table tbody th {
      width: 2.6rem;
      font-size: 0.68rem;
      padding-right: 0.3rem;
    }

    .cal-total {
      width: 2rem;
      font-size: 0.68rem;
    }
  }

  /* ---- Monthly output bars ---- */

  .month-bars {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-end;
    gap: 6px;
    height: 130px;
  }

  .month-bar {
    flex: 1;
    height: 100%;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: flex-end;
    gap: 2px;
    position: relative;
  }

  .month-bar-seg {
    display: block;
    min-height: 2px;
    border-radius: 2px 2px 0 0;
    -webkit-print-color-adjust: exact;
    print-color-adjust: exact;
  }

  .month-bar-seg--blog { background: var(--stats-accent); }
  .month-bar-seg--note { background: var(--stats-accent-soft); }

  /* Hidden below 700px: under that width the panels either sit in one column
     (labels are redundant against the wide bars) or squeeze into the tight
     two-column band where adjacent labels would touch. */
  .month-bar-label {
    display: none;
  }

  @media (min-width: 700px) {
    .month-bar-label {
      display: block;
      position: absolute;
      bottom: -1.1rem;
      left: 50%;
      transform: translateX(-50%);
      font-family: var(--font-family-monospace);
      font-size: 0.6rem;
      color: var(--text-color-soft);
    }
  }

  .bar-caption {
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0;
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--text-color-soft);
  }

  .bar-caption .key {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    margin-right: 1.25rem;
  }

  .bar-caption .key b {
    width: 10px;
    height: 10px;
    border-radius: 2px;
    -webkit-print-color-adjust: exact;
    print-color-adjust: exact;
  }

  .bar-caption .key--blog b { background: var(--stats-accent); }
  .bar-caption .key--note b { background: var(--stats-accent-soft); }

  /* ---- Horizontal labelled bars (weekdays, hours) ---- */

  .bar-rows {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .bar-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 2.6rem 1fr 2.2rem;
    align-items: center;
    column-gap: 0.6rem;
  }

  .bar-row-key {
    font-family: var(--font-family-monospace);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--text-color-soft);
  }

  .bar-row-track {
    height: 8px;
    border-radius: 100px;
    background: var(--stats-empty);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .bar-row-fill {
    display: block;
    height: 100%;
    border-radius: 100px;
    background: var(--stats-accent-soft);
    -webkit-print-color-adjust: exact;
    print-color-adjust: exact;
  }

  .bar-row--peak .bar-row-fill {
    background: var(--stats-accent);
  }

  .bar-row-val {
    font-family: var(--font-family-monospace);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--text-color-soft);
    text-align: right;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  /* ---- Tags ---- */

  /* Twenty stacked full-width bars made the page's longest, most monotonous
     stretch. The same information fits in a few rows as chips: each one is the
     link to its tag page, carries its count, and fills from the left in
     proportion to that count, so the ranking is still readable at a glance. */
  .tag-chips {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(min(170px, 100%), 1fr));
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .tag-chip {
    --fill: 0%;
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    padding: 0.45rem 0.7rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
    border-radius: 6px;
    max-width: none;
    text-decoration: none;
    color: inherit;
    background:
      linear-gradient(to right, var(--stats-accent-faint) var(--fill), transparent var(--fill)),
      var(--surface-color);
  }

  .tag-chip:hover,
  .tag-chip:focus-visible {
    border-color: var(--stats-accent-soft);
  }

  .tag-chip-name {
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    overflow: hidden;
    text-overflow: ellipsis;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .tag-chip:hover .tag-chip-name,
  .tag-chip:focus-visible .tag-chip-name {
    color: var(--text-color-link);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }

  .tag-chip-count {
    font-family: var(--font-family-monospace);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--text-color-soft);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  /* ---- GitHub ---- */

  .gh-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 520px) {
    .gh-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }

  .gh-chart-card {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
    padding: 1.1rem 1.25rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: var(--surface-color);
  }

  .gh-chart-card p {
    margin: 0 0 0.8rem;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--text-color-muted);
  }

  /* Real bars rather than Unicode blocks: same visual language as every other
     chart on the page, and each week keeps its own tooltip. */
  .gh-weeks {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-end;
    gap: 2px;
    height: 70px;
  }

  .gh-week {
    flex: 1;
    min-width: 0;
    border-radius: 2px 2px 0 0;
    background: var(--stats-accent-soft);
    -webkit-print-color-adjust: exact;
    print-color-adjust: exact;
  }

  .gh-axis {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    font-family: var(--font-family-monospace);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    color: var(--text-color-soft);
    margin-top: 0.45rem;
  }

  /* Fallback when a cached snapshot predates the weekly series. */
  .gh-spark {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--font-family-monospace);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    letter-spacing: 1px;
    line-height: 1.3;
    color: var(--text-color-link);
    white-space: pre-wrap;
    word-break: break-all;
  }

  /* ---- Tables ---- */

  /* Scroll shadows: the two `local` layers paint the page background over the
     shadows at rest, and the `scroll` layers stay pinned to the edges, so a
     shadow appears only on the side that has more content off-screen. Without
     this a clipped column looks like the table simply ends. */
  .stats-table-wrap {
    overflow-x: auto;
    background:
      linear-gradient(to right, var(--background-color) 30%, transparent) left center / 3rem 100% no-repeat local,
      linear-gradient(to left, var(--background-color) 30%, transparent) right center / 3rem 100% no-repeat local,
      radial-gradient(farthest-side at 0 50%, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.16), transparent) left center / 1rem 100% no-repeat scroll,
      radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 50%, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.16), transparent) right center / 1rem 100% no-repeat scroll;
    overscroll-behavior-x: contain;
  }

  .stats-table {
    display: table;
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  .stats-table th,
  .stats-table td {
    padding: 0.55rem 0.85rem;
    text-align: right;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color);
  }

  .stats-table thead th {
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text-color-soft);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color-strong);
  }

  .stats-table tbody th {
    text-align: left;
    font-family: var(--font-family-monospace);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text-color-muted);
  }

  .stats-table tbody tr:nth-child(even) {
    background: var(--table-row-even);
  }

  /* The share column is the row's own volume against the biggest year, split
     into posts and notes – it replaces a year-on-year percentage that read as
     a collapse whenever a format was simply introduced or retired. */
  .stats-table .col-share {
    width: 30%;
    min-width: 90px;
  }

  .share-bar {
    display: flex;
    height: 8px;
    border-radius: 100px;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--stats-empty);
  }

  /* A year with a handful of entries still gets a visible sliver rather than
     rounding away to an empty track. */
  .share-bar span {
    height: 100%;
    min-width: 3px;
    -webkit-print-color-adjust: exact;
    print-color-adjust: exact;
  }

  .share-bar .share-blog { background: var(--stats-accent); }
  .share-bar .share-note { background: var(--stats-accent-soft); }

  /* On a phone the two widest columns go rather than making a six-column table
     scroll sideways. Words and share are the reference detail; the counts are
     the point. */
  @media (max-width: 559px) {
    .stats-table .col-words,
    .stats-table .col-share {
      display: none;
    }

    .stats-table th,
    .stats-table td {
      padding: 0.5rem 0.5rem;
    }
  }

  .stats-empty-note {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--text-color-soft);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  .stats-table-note {
    margin: 0.75rem 0 0;
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--text-color-soft);
  }

  .stats-footer-note {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    padding-top: 1.25rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-color);
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: var(--text-color-soft);
  }

  @media (max-width: 520px) {
    .month-bars {
      gap: 4px;
    }
  }

  /* ---- Print ---- */

  @media print {
    .stats-hero {
      margin-top: 0;
    }

    /* Nothing on paper is clickable, so the accent stops carrying meaning. */
    .hero-figure,
    .stat-number {
      color: inherit;
    }

    .panel,
    .stat-card,
    .gh-chart-card,
    .cal-wrap,
    .stats-table-wrap {
      break-inside: avoid;
    }

    .stat-card,
    .gh-chart-card,
    .tag-chip {
      background: none;
    }

    .stats-table-wrap {
      overflow: visible;
      background: none;
    }
  }
</style>

<div class="stats">
	<h1>{{ title }}</h1>

	<p>Everything this site knows about itself, recounted from the source files on every build.</p>

	{#- Aggregates used in more than one place below (books, projects, blogroll feeds). -#}
	{% set booksDone = 0 %}{% set booksReading = 0 %}{% set booksPlanned = 0 %}
	{% for b in books %}{% if b.status == "completed" %}{% set booksDone = booksDone + 1 %}{% elif b.status == "reading" %}{% set booksReading = booksReading + 1 %}{% else %}{% set booksPlanned = booksPlanned + 1 %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
	{% set projActive = 0 %}{% set projStable = 0 %}{% set projOther = 0 %}{% set projMini = 0 %}
	{% for p in projects.projects %}{% if p.type == 'mini' %}{% set projMini = projMini + 1 %}{% elif p.status == 'active' %}{% set projActive = projActive + 1 %}{% elif p.status == 'stable' %}{% set projStable = projStable + 1 %}{% else %}{% set projOther = projOther + 1 %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
	{% set blogrollFeeds = 0 %}{% for b in blogroll %}{% if b.feed %}{% set blogrollFeeds = blogrollFeeds + 1 %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
	{% set yearsWriting = (siteStats.daysSinceFirst / 365.25) | round(1) %}
	{% set ytd = siteStats.yearToDate %}

	<div class="stats-hero">
		<span class="hero-figure">{{ siteStats.totals.wordsAll | toLocaleString }}</span>
		<span class="hero-label">words published</span>
		<p class="hero-note">Across <a href="/archive/">{{ siteStats.totals.entries }} posts and notes</a> written over {{ yearsWriting }} years, starting {{ siteStats.first.date }}, plus {{ siteStats.totals.pageCount }} standalone pages. That is {{ siteStats.readingLabel }} of reading.</p>
	</div>

	<ul class="stat-row">
		<li>
			<span class="stat-row-fig">{{ ytd.entries }}</span>
			<span class="stat-row-label">entries so far in {{ ytd.year }}</span>
			<span class="stat-row-sub">{{ ytd.lastYearEntries }} by this date in {{ ytd.lastYear }}</span>
		</li>
		<li>
			{#- Early in a new year there are not yet two entries to measure a pace
			    from, so the figure falls back to the all-time one rather than
			    rendering blank. -#}
			{% if ytd.pace %}
			<span class="stat-row-fig">{{ ytd.pace }}</span>
			<span class="stat-row-label">days between entries this year</span>
			<span class="stat-row-sub">{{ siteStats.avgDaysBetween }} across the whole run</span>
			{% else %}
			<span class="stat-row-fig">{{ siteStats.avgDaysBetween }}</span>
			<span class="stat-row-label">days between entries</span>
			<span class="stat-row-sub">across the whole run</span>
			{% endif %}
		</li>
		<li>
			{#- An absolute date rather than "today" or "3 days ago". The site only
			    rebuilds when something is published, so a relative phrase is frozen
			    at the moment of the last build and quietly becomes wrong the next
			    day. A date stays true however long the gap runs. -#}
			<a href="{{ siteStats.latest.url }}">
				<span class="stat-row-fig">{{ siteStats.latest.dateShort }}</span>
				<span class="stat-row-label">last published</span>
				<span class="stat-row-sub">{{ siteStats.latest.title }}</span>
			</a>
		</li>
	</ul>

	<h2 id="output">Output over time</h2>
	<p class="section-intro">Posts are the long-form pieces; notes are the short ones.</p>

	<h3>Every month since the beginning</h3>
	<p>Shaded by how busy each month was. Pick any month to open it in the archive.</p>
	<div class="cal-wrap" data-table-wrap>
		<table class="cal-table">
			<caption class="visually-hidden">Entries published in each month, by year, newest year first.</caption>
			<thead>
				<tr>
					<th scope="col"><span class="visually-hidden">Year</span></th>
					{% for label in ["Jan","Feb","Mar","Apr","May","Jun","Jul","Aug","Sep","Oct","Nov","Dec"] %}
					<th scope="col"><span aria-hidden="true">{{ label[0] }}</span><span class="visually-hidden">{{ label }}</span></th>
					{% endfor %}
					<th scope="col"><span class="visually-hidden">Year total</span></th>
				</tr>
			</thead>
			<tbody>
				{% for y in siteStats.calendar %}
				<tr>
					{#- A year with no entries has no archive page generated for it, so
					    the label is only a link when there is something to open. -#}
					<th scope="row">{% if y.totalCount %}<a href="/archive/{{ y.year }}/">{{ y.year }}</a>{% else %}{{ y.year }}{% endif %}</th>
					{% for m in y.months %}
					<td>
						{%- if m.count == 0 -%}
						<span class="cal-cell" aria-label="{{ m.short }} {{ y.year }}: nothing"><span class="cal-num">·</span></span>
						{%- else -%}
						<a class="cal-cell cal-cell--c{{ m.level }}" href="{{ m.anchor }}" aria-label="{{ m.short }} {{ y.year }}: {{ m.count }} entr{{ 'y' if m.count == 1 else 'ies' }}"><span class="cal-num">{{ m.count }}</span></a>
						{%- endif -%}
					</td>
					{% endfor %}
					<td class="cal-total">{{ y.totalCount }}</td>
				</tr>
				{% endfor %}
			</tbody>
		</table>
	</div>
	<div class="cal-legend" aria-hidden="true">
		<span>entries per month:</span>
		<span><b style="background: var(--stats-empty)"></b>0</span>
		{% for step in siteStats.heatLegend %}<span><b style="background: var(--heat-{{ step.level }})"></b>{{ step.label }}</span>{% endfor %}
	</div>
	<p class="cal-readout">The busiest single month was {{ siteStats.busiestMonth }}, and the current run is {{ siteStats.streaks.current }} months without a gap. Shading steps are quintiles of the months that have entries, so the colour splits where the data actually sits.</p>

	<h3>Year by year</h3>
	<div class="reference">
		<div class="stats-table-wrap" data-table-wrap>
			<table class="stats-table">
				<thead>
					<tr>
						<th scope="col">Year</th>
						<th scope="col">Posts</th>
						<th scope="col">Notes</th>
						<th scope="col">Total</th>
						<th scope="col" class="col-words">Words</th>
						<th scope="col" class="col-share">Share of biggest year</th>
					</tr>
				</thead>
				<tbody>
					{% for y in siteStats.yearRows %}
					<tr>
						<th scope="row">{{ y.year }}</th>
						<td>{{ y.blog }}</td>
						<td>{{ y.note }}</td>
						<td>{{ y.total }}</td>
						<td class="col-words">{{ y.words | toLocaleString }}</td>
						<td class="col-share">
							<div class="share-bar" role="img" aria-label="{{ y.blog }} posts and {{ y.note }} notes">
								{% if y.blog > 0 %}<span class="share-blog" style="width: {{ y.barBlog }}%"></span>{% endif %}
								{% if y.note > 0 %}<span class="share-note" style="width: {{ y.barNote }}%"></span>{% endif %}
							</div>
						</td>
					</tr>
					{% endfor %}
				</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>
		<p class="stats-table-note">Bars compare each year against the biggest one, split into posts and notes.{% if siteStats.bestYear %} The biggest complete year so far is {{ siteStats.bestYear.year }}, with {{ siteStats.bestYear.total }} entries.{% endif %} {{ ytd.year }} is still in progress.</p>
	</div>

	<h2 id="rhythm">Writing rhythm</h2>
	<p class="section-intro">Not how much, but when – the pace it keeps and the days and hours things actually get published.</p>
	<div class="panel-grid">
		<div class="panel">
			<h3>Pace and streak</h3>
			<ul class="figure-list">
				<li><span class="figure-key">current streak</span><span class="figure-val">{{ siteStats.streaks.current }} months</span></li>
				<li><span class="figure-key">longest streak</span><span class="figure-val">{{ siteStats.streaks.longest }} months</span></li>
				<li><span class="figure-key">busiest month</span><span class="figure-val">{{ siteStats.busiestMonth }}</span></li>
				<li><span class="figure-key">longest silence</span><span class="figure-val">{{ siteStats.gaps.longestDays }} days</span></li>
				<li><span class="figure-key">first post</span><span class="figure-val">{{ siteStats.first.date }}</span></li>
			</ul>
			<p class="card-note">A streak counts consecutive months with at least one entry.</p>
		</div>
		<div class="panel">
			<h3>This year so far ({{ siteStats.calendar[0].year }})</h3>
			{% set yr = siteStats.calendar[0] %}
			{#- The two segments stack, so the scale is the biggest monthly total –
			    scaling each segment against its own maximum would let a bar run
			    past the top of the chart. -#}
			{% set chartMax = 1 %}
			{% for m in yr.months %}{% if m.count > chartMax %}{% set chartMax = m.count %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
			<div class="month-bars" role="img" aria-label="Posts and notes per month in {{ yr.year }}: {{ yr.totalCount }} total">
				{% for m in yr.months %}
				<div class="month-bar" title="{{ m.short }} {{ yr.year }} · {{ m.blog }} post{{ '' if m.blog == 1 else 's' }}, {{ m.note }} note{{ '' if m.note == 1 else 's' }}">
					{% if m.blog > 0 %}<span class="month-bar-seg month-bar-seg--blog" style="height: {{ (m.blog / chartMax * 100) | round(0) }}%"></span>{% endif %}
					{% if m.note > 0 %}<span class="month-bar-seg month-bar-seg--note" style="height: {{ (m.note / chartMax * 100) | round(0) }}%"></span>{% endif %}
					<span class="month-bar-label" aria-hidden="true">{{ m.short }}</span>
				</div>
				{% endfor %}
			</div>
			<p class="bar-caption">
				<span class="key key--blog"><b></b>posts</span>
				<span class="key key--note"><b></b>notes</span>
			</p>
			<p class="card-note">{{ yr.totalCount }} entries so far this year. Bars are stacked and scaled to the busiest month of the year, at {{ chartMax }}.</p>
		</div>
		<div class="panel">
			<h3>Day of the week</h3>
			{% set peakWeekday = siteStats.weekdays[0] %}
			<div class="bar-rows">
				{% for d in siteStats.weekdayBars %}
				<div class="bar-row{{ ' bar-row--peak' if d.count == peakWeekday.count }}">
					<span class="bar-row-key">{{ d.label }}</span>
					<span class="bar-row-track"><span class="bar-row-fill" style="width: {{ d.pct }}%"></span></span>
					<span class="bar-row-val">{{ d.count }}</span>
				</div>
				{% endfor %}
			</div>
			<p class="card-note">{{ peakWeekday.count }} entries went out on {{ peakWeekday.label }}, more than any other day.</p>
		</div>
		<div class="panel reference">
			<h3>Time of day</h3>
			<div class="bar-rows">
				{% set maxHourCount = 0 %}
				{% for h in siteStats.hourBars %}{% if h.count > maxHourCount %}{% set maxHourCount = h.count %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
				{% for h in siteStats.hourBars %}
				<div class="bar-row{{ ' bar-row--peak' if h.count == maxHourCount }}">
					<span class="bar-row-key">{{ h.label }}</span>
					<span class="bar-row-track"><span class="bar-row-fill" style="width: {{ h.pct }}%"></span></span>
					<span class="bar-row-val">{{ h.count }}</span>
				</div>
				{% endfor %}
			</div>
			<p class="card-note">Publish times in {{ metadata.timezone }}, grouped into four-hour bands. The three busiest hours are {{ siteStats.topHours | join(", ") }}.</p>
		</div>
	</div>

	<h2 id="inside">Inside the writing</h2>
	<p class="section-intro">What the {{ siteStats.totals.entries | toLocaleString }} entries are actually made of.</p>
	<div class="panel-grid panel-grid--stack">
		<div class="panel">
			<h3>Typical lengths</h3>
			<ul class="figure-list">
				<li><span class="figure-key">median entry</span><span class="figure-val">{{ siteStats.extremes.medianWords | toLocaleString }} words</span></li>
				<li><span class="figure-key">average post</span><span class="figure-val">{{ siteStats.averages.wordsPerPost | toLocaleString }} words</span></li>
				<li><span class="figure-key">average note</span><span class="figure-val">{{ siteStats.averages.wordsPerNote | toLocaleString }} words</span></li>
				<li><span class="figure-key">posts + notes</span><span class="figure-val">{{ siteStats.totals.wordsTotal | toLocaleString }} words</span></li>
			</ul>
			<p class="card-note">The range runs from <a href="{{ siteStats.extremes.shortest.url }}">{{ siteStats.extremes.shortest.title }}</a> at {{ siteStats.extremes.shortest.words }} words to <a href="{{ siteStats.extremes.longest.url }}">{{ siteStats.extremes.longest.title }}</a> at {{ siteStats.extremes.longest.words | toLocaleString }}. This panel is posts and notes only, and quotes each entry the way its own page does. The headline total of {{ siteStats.totals.wordsAll | toLocaleString }} words also counts standalone pages, build-log entries, and image alt text, which is written but never rendered – so per-post figures do not add up to it exactly.</p>
		</div>
		<div class="panel">
			<h3>What is embedded</h3>
			<ul class="figure-list">
				<li><span class="figure-key">images</span><span class="figure-val">{{ siteStats.totals.images | toLocaleString }}</span></li>
				<li><span class="figure-key">code blocks</span><span class="figure-val">{{ siteStats.totals.codeBlocks }}</span></li>
				<li><span class="figure-key">lines of code</span><span class="figure-val">{{ siteStats.totals.codeLines | toLocaleString }}</span></li>
				<li><span class="figure-key">self-hosted videos</span><span class="figure-val">{{ siteStats.totals.videoPosts }}</span></li>
			</ul>
			<p class="card-note">Images appear in {{ siteStats.totals.postsWithImages }} entries and code in {{ siteStats.totals.postsWithCode }}, roughly {{ siteStats.averages.codeSharePct }}% of everything published here.</p>
		</div>
		<div class="panel reference">
			<h3>Upkeep and reach</h3>
			<ul class="figure-list">
				<li><span class="figure-key">revised entries</span><span class="figure-val">{{ siteStats.freshness.updatedCount }}</span></li>
				<li><span class="figure-key">revised after</span><span class="figure-val">{{ siteStats.freshness.avgDaysToUpdate }} days</span></li>
				<li><span class="figure-key">on Mastodon</span><span class="figure-val">{{ siteStats.totals.mastodonPosts }}</span></li>
				<li><span class="figure-key">tags per entry</span><span class="figure-val">{{ siteStats.tags.avgPerEntry }}</span></li>
			</ul>
			<p class="card-note">Revised entries carry an updated date, shown on the post itself. The revision figure is an average across those {{ siteStats.freshness.updatedCount }} entries.</p>
		</div>
	</div>

	<h2 id="tags">Tags</h2>
	{% set topTags = collections | getAllTagsDetails | head(24) %}
	<p class="section-intro">{{ siteStats.tags.distinct }} tags are in use and {{ siteStats.tags.singleUse }} of them appear exactly once. These are the {{ topTags | length }} biggest, sized by how often each is used.</p>
	{% set maxTag = topTags[0].count if topTags | length else 1 %}
	{% set shownTotal = 0 %}
	{% for tag in topTags %}{% set shownTotal = shownTotal + tag.count %}{% endfor %}
	{#- Chips rather than a stack of full-width bars: each one fills from the left
	    in proportion to its count, so the ranking still reads at a glance in a
	    fifth of the height. -#}
	<div class="tag-chips">
		{% for tag in topTags %}
		<a class="tag-chip" href="/tags/{{ tag.name | slugify }}/" style="--fill: {{ (tag.count / maxTag * 100) | round(1) }}%">
			<span class="tag-chip-name">{{ tag.name }}</span>
			<span class="tag-chip-count">{{ tag.count }}</span>
		</a>
		{% endfor %}
	</div>
	<p class="stats-table-note">{% if siteStats.tags.assignments %}The {{ topTags | length }} tags above account for {{ (shownTotal / siteStats.tags.assignments * 100) | round(0) }}% of all tag uses. {% endif %}<a href="/tags/">Browse all {{ siteStats.tags.distinct }} tags</a>.</p>

	{%- if metadata.githubUsername %}
	<h2 id="github">GitHub</h2>
	{%- if githubActivity %}
	<p class="section-intro">The other half of the output: code pushed over the last {{ githubActivity.totalDays }} days.</p>
	<div class="gh-grid">
		<div class="stat-card">
			<span class="stat-number">{{ githubActivity.total | toLocaleString }}</span>
			<span class="stat-label">total contributions</span>
			{% if githubActivity.avgPerActiveDay %}<span class="stat-sub">{{ githubActivity.avgPerActiveDay }} per active day</span>{% endif %}
		</div>
		<div class="stat-card">
			<span class="stat-number">{{ githubActivity.activeDays }}</span>
			<span class="stat-label">active days</span>
			<span class="stat-sub">of {{ githubActivity.totalDays }} days</span>
		</div>
		<div class="stat-card">
			<span class="stat-number">{{ githubActivity.currentStreak }}</span>
			<span class="stat-label">current streak (days)</span>
			<span class="stat-sub">best {{ githubActivity.bestStreak }}</span>
		</div>
		<div class="stat-card">
			<span class="stat-number">{{ githubActivity.busiestCount }}</span>
			<span class="stat-label">busiest day</span>
			<span class="stat-sub">{{ githubActivity.busiestLabel or githubActivity.busiestDate }}</span>
		</div>
		<div class="gh-chart-card">
			<p>Contributions per week, scaled against the busiest week.</p>
			{%- if githubActivity.weekBars %}
			<div class="gh-weeks" role="img" aria-label="Weekly GitHub contributions from {{ githubActivity.startLabel }} to {{ githubActivity.endLabel }}, {{ githubActivity.total }} in total">
				{% for w in githubActivity.weekBars %}<span class="gh-week" style="height: {{ w.pct }}%" title="Week of {{ w.label }} · {{ w.total }} contribution{{ '' if w.total == 1 else 's' }}"></span>{% endfor %}
			</div>
			{%- else %}
			<span class="gh-spark" aria-hidden="true">{{ githubActivity.sparkline }}</span>
			{%- endif %}
			<span class="gh-axis"><span>{{ githubActivity.startLabel }}</span><span>{{ githubActivity.endLabel }}</span></span>
		</div>
	</div>
	{%- else %}
	<p class="stats-empty-note">GitHub stats were unavailable on this build – the page falls back to a cached snapshot, so try again later.</p>
	{%- endif %}

	{%- endif %}

	<h2 id="collections">Collections</h2>
	<p class="section-intro">Everything else the site keeps a list of. Each card opens its page.</p>
	<div class="collection-grid">
		<a class="stat-card" href="/books/">
			<span class="stat-number">{{ books | length }}</span>
			<span class="stat-label">books</span>
			<span class="stat-sub">{{ booksDone }} read · {{ booksReading }} reading · {{ booksPlanned }} planned</span>
		</a>
		<a class="stat-card" href="/projects/">
			<span class="stat-number">{{ projects.projects | length }}</span>
			<span class="stat-label">projects</span>
			<span class="stat-sub">{{ projActive }} active · {{ projStable }} stable · {{ projMini }} mini</span>
		</a>
		<a class="stat-card" href="/blogroll/">
			<span class="stat-number">{{ blogroll | length }}</span>
			<span class="stat-label">blogs in the blogroll</span>
			<span class="stat-sub">{{ blogrollFeeds }} with a public feed</span>
		</a>
		<a class="stat-card" href="/bookmarks/">
			<span class="stat-number">{{ bookmarks | length }}</span>
			<span class="stat-label">bookmarks</span>
			<span class="stat-sub">links kept for later</span>
		</a>
		<a class="stat-card" href="/changelog/">
			<span class="stat-number">{{ changelog | length }}</span>
			<span class="stat-label">site changes logged</span>
			<span class="stat-sub">every notable change to this site</span>
		</a>
	</div>

	<p class="stats-footer-note">Counted on {{ siteStats.builtOn }}, the last time the site was built. Anything measured against "this year" or "to date" is as of then. Every figure comes from the source files, not from analytics. See <a href="/colophon/">how this site is built</a>.</p>
</div>
